! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! Bisbas et al. (2015) sec 5.4 H II region + PDR at the OWNERSHIP CONTRACT.
!
!   MOCASSIN -> 3D-PDR   ion densities, Ne, Te, dust temperature, dust opacity
!   3D-PDR -> MOCASSIN   molecular content + the heating/cooling that follows
!   MOCASSIN owns        ionization, thermal equilibrium, molecular bookkeeping
!
! D-196. Every keyword below states a piece of that contract that the
! compiled defaults get backwards. They are keywords here because that is
! what the code currently offers; under the contract most of them have
! exactly one correct value and should become the design, not an input
! line (CLAUDE.md: "ownership is a design decision and belongs in the
! design, not in an input keyword"). This fixture is the bridge - it makes
! the target state reproducible from the repository before the switches
! are collapsed, so the collapse can be verified against something.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
TStellar 40000.
contShape blackbody
LPhot 4.26e13
symmetricXYZ
Hdensity 100.
nebComposition "input/abunV1.in"
TeStart 8000.
maxIterateMC 12 95.
nPhotons 6000000
nx 31
ny 31
nz 31
nbins 600
nuMax 15.
nuMin 1.001e-5
Rin 30.e17
Rout 6.0e19
edges 6.0e19 6.0e19 6.0e19
convLimit 0.10
dustFile 'input/dust_species.dat' 'input/dust_sizes.dat'
MdMg constant 0.011295
pdr 1
pdrDataDir "/home/hmonteiro/software/mocassin_HM_2026_3DPDR/dataPDR"
pdrNetwork "reduced"
pdrZeta 5.0e-17
pdrCoolants 4 "12co.dat" "12c+.dat" "12c.dat" "16o.dat"
pdrStartIter 4

! ---- MOCASSIN owns the ionization ------------------------------------
! Its ratio is imposed on the network before and after each solve (D-162).
! This also disables the pdrOwnIon gate (D-169), which otherwise makes
! ionBalance skip H, He, C, O and Mg outright in every PDR-zone cell.
pdrIonFromMocassin 1
! Explicit, though redundant while the line above is set: MOCASSIN solves
! the ionization of every element, everywhere.
pdrOwnIon 0

! ---- MOCASSIN owns the thermal equilibrium ---------------------------
! The PDR stops solving for T and stops writing grid%Te; MOCASSIN's
! thermBalance solves it, which it can only do honestly if it also
! receives the PDR's budget - the next two lines are not separable from
! this one.
pdrTeFromMocassin 1
! The molecular coolants MOCASSIN has no line data for, and the six
! heating terms it has no expression for, reach thermBalance.
pdrCoolFeedback 1
! ...and reach it as a FUNCTION of T, not a constant. In neutral gas the
! PDR coolant is the only term without a factor n_e, so held constant
! inside iterateT it leaves H-C with no root and the search runs to a
! rail - D-166 measured 45% of the model pinned at 30000 K or 10 K.
pdrCoolTdep 1

! ---- MOCASSIN owns the molecular bookkeeping -------------------------
! elemAvail - the fraction of each element NOT locked in molecules -
! carries the locking, instead of standing down wherever the chemistry
! supplied per-stage rates (D-118). The rates enter the ion matrix as a
! source and a sink; they do not constrain the conservation row, so with
! the stand-down active that row asserts x(H0) + x(H+) = 1 in gas that is
! 98% molecular. See D-196.
ionChemRates 0
! MOCASSIN's own electron density is what ionBalance uses.
pdrUseNePDR 0

! ---- no zone --------------------------------------------------------
! The chemistry runs in every cell. Outside the molecular gas it answers
! "no molecules here" by itself and needs no threshold to be switched off;
! with the gate in place H2 and CO were zero in ionized gas because
! nothing had computed them, not because the chemistry said so (D-131).
pdrAllCells 1
